6 outs to make a pair might not even be good enough if they have two pair or better. Calling 156 for roughly 30% pot odds when I likely have less than 15% equity is -EV. Bluff-raising is too risky with a hand this weak on the turn. The disciplined play is to fold and preserve chips for better spots in the remaining 6 hands.\n\nAnswer: -1"}
