t heavily to a marginal hand.\n\nThe aggressive re-raise from my opponent is a strong signal. Calling to see the river is risky because:\n- If an Ace, 9, or club comes, I'm likely beaten\n- Even if a blank comes, they may bet big on the river\n- I'd be putting more chips at risk with a mediocre holding\n\n**Folding here** allows me to:\n- Preserve my 19,450 chips\n- Have a full stack (20,000) for the crucial final hand\n- Avoid a potentially costly confrontation with a marginal hand\n\nThis is the disciplined play given the circumstances.\n\n# Answer: -1"}
